# Verification

## Desk (`kit/studio/`)

Before merging or saying a desk change is ready:

```bash
cd kit/studio && npm run verify   # typecheck → lint → test → build
```

Node **20.19+** for the test toolchain. Dev loop: repo root `./studio --dev` (server `:4747`, Vite `:4748`).

## Kit / CLI (repo root)

```bash
node --test kit/lib/*.test.mjs kit/lib/shared/*.test.js scripts/*.test.mjs
```

Touch shared modules in **`kit/lib/shared/`** when logic is used by both engine and desk; keep **`kit/lib/shared/*.js`** and TS ports in sync.

## When to add or extend tests

- Timeline, plate editor, copy edit, magnifier, scrub, parity with render → extend **`kit/studio/src/features/editor/**`** tests or **`kit/studio/src/logic/*.test.ts`**.
- Narration/script/flow/agent/critic → **`kit/lib/*.test.mjs`**, **`narrationQc`**, etc.

## Visual / interaction bugs

- Reproduce on a **named slug** the user gave (or a standard demo project).
- Scrub **forward and back** across slides; toggle **Program ↔ Editor**; toggle **edit text / magnifier**—many bugs only appear after navigation.
- After engine changes, hard-reload or confirm Vite HMR picked up **`plate.ts`** / engine modules (stale bundle mimics unfixed bugs).
- See **`common-regressions.mdc`** for the symptom → cause matrix (shrink-on-scrub-back, white flash on edit, transition flash, frozen LIVE).

## Standard repro slugs

- `browse-hacker-news-like-a-pro` — live capture, streaming, timeline
- `walkthrough-studio` — full Render / produce path, pipeline perf
- `teamdeck-dla-agencji-designu` — project-specific perf / re-record issues
- Apptension marketing walkthrough — transition flash at chapter boundaries

## Browser / desk

- Prefer **`./studio --dev`** and **4748** for editor work; server API on **4747**.
- Optional: Playwright **`kit/studio/e2e`** against stub studio for regressions on ids/shortcuts.
- **`npm run test:coverage`** when changing shared UI with thresholds.

## Debugging discipline

- On “**still** broken”: restate repro, identify **first wrong frame/event**, fix root cause (often cache/lifecycle), add test if pure logic.
- Systematic-debugging skill applies for non-obvious desk bugs — hypothesis → instrument → confirm before large refactors.

## Performance work

- Profile or measure before large changes; **no intentional behavior change** unless fixing a bug.
- Prefer fewer DOM rebuilds, narrower store subscriptions, and debounced preview updates over micro-optimizations that risk parity bugs.
